# Headhunter Agent (Agent 5)

## Identity

* **Type:** In-process Python daemon (same pattern as Aligner).
* **Role:** Unified VCS lifecycle automation (`GitLabPlatform` + `GitHubPlatform` implementing `VcsPlatformPort` in `src/agents/headhunter_port.py`). Polls GitLab `/todos` + bounded `darwin:gitlab:mr_sha` sweep and GitHub PRs/Issues/review-feedback, classifies items, and creates/wakes events for Brain.
* **Behavior:** Autonomous, FIFO. Processes oldest queued/discovered items first via shared Phase A/B engine. Does NOT route to agents directly -- creates events or appends active-event wake-ups for Brain.

## Architecture

* **Core Files:** `src/agents/headhunter.py` (orchestrator), `src/agents/headhunter_port.py` (`VcsPlatformPort` Protocol), `src/agents/headhunter_models.py` (stdlib-only canonical dataclasses), `src/agents/headhunter_utils.py` (zero-import shared sanitizers/helpers), `src/agents/headhunter_gitlab.py`, `src/agents/headhunter_github.py`.
* **Pattern:** Poll (GitLab + GitHub via `VcsPlatformPort`) -> Flow Gate -> Classify -> Create Event / Active Wake-Up -> Brain handles routing -> Three-Phase Close Feedback.
* **LLM:** gemini-4-argon via `_get_adapter()` (env: `LLM_MODEL_HEADHUNTER`, `LLM_TEMPERATURE_HEADHUNTER`, `LLM_MAX_TOKENS_HEADHUNTER`). System instructions loaded from `headhunter_skills/` (`gitlab-mr-triage.md`, `github-pr-triage.md`, `github-pr-review-response.md`, `github-issue-triage.md`).
* **Flow Gate:** Global WIP cap (`MAX_ACTIVE_EVENTS`) controls event creation. Headhunter's `check_flow_gate()` queries the global WIP count via injected `Brain.count_global_wip(include_new=True)` (or local fallback), which subtracts `_waiting_for_user` events to free capacity for incoming work. When full, `VcsPlatformPort.queue_item()` parks work items (GitLab atomic Redis FIFO `darwin:gitlab:queue`, GitHub `darwin-queued` label) instead of dropping them.
* **Circuit Breaker:** Per-platform (`gitlab`, `github`) half-open circuit breaker in `headhunter.py`. 3 consecutive failures -> `open` (cooldown -> `half_open` probe -> `closed`). Exposed via `Headhunter.gitlab_breaker_state` / `github_breaker_state` and `GET /queue/headhunter/status`.
* **Snapshot Persistence:** At end of every poll cycle, Headhunter persists redacted per-platform `PlatformSnapshot` JSON to Redis (`darwin:headhunter:snapshot:{platform}`, TTL `3 * poll_interval` / `900s`, errors redacted + capped `<= 200` chars).
* **Startup Delay:** 180s default (env: `HEADHUNTER_STARTUP_DELAY`). Waits for sidecars.

## LLM Analysis

All MRs/PRs go through gemini-4-argon analysis with system instructions from `headhunter_skills/`. The SI defines output format (YAML frontmatter matching `create_plan` schema, validated with `yaml.safe_load()`), domain classification, agent assignment, risk assessment, and downstream Brain awareness.

| Path | Trigger | How |
|---|---|---|
| **LLM Analysis** | MRs / PRs / Issues | gemini-4-argon reads full context (description, pipeline/checks, changed files, comments) and generates a YAML plan. Description capped by `HEADHUNTER_DESCRIPTION_CAP` (default `100000`). Bot/DARWIN Instructions in the description are included as prompt context. Output controlled by `LLM_MAX_TOKENS_HEADHUNTER`. |
| **Emergency Fallback** | LLM unavailable | Inline `_emergency_plan()` produces COMPLICATED/developer plan (with JSON-quoted scalars). Safety net only. |

## Maintainer Resolution

Chain: `HEADHUNTER_MAINTAINERS` (static CSV) -> GitLab/GitHub email or metadata lookup -> fallback.

* Static list is read at runtime (not import time) via `_get_static_maintainer_emails()`.
* Resolved maintainer stored in `evidence.gitlab_context.maintainer` / `evidence.github_context.maintainer` / `evidence.github_issue_context.maintainer` at event creation.

## Security: @Mention Instruction Injection & SHA Drift Hardening

* MR/PR comments tagging the configured bot account (`GITLAB_BOT_USERNAME` on GitLab, `@{GITHUB_APP_SLUG}` on GitHub) are passed as plan context only after passing fail-closed trust checks.
* **GitLab allowlist:** email local parts from `HEADHUNTER_MAINTAINERS` + explicit `HEADHUNTER_ALLOWED_AUTHORS` CSV. If both are empty, all `@mentions` are blocked (`_nobody_` sentinel); proven-unauthorized `@mention` todos are dismissed individually during poll without affecting authorized sibling todos.
* **GitHub trust gate:** `author_association` in `HEADHUNTER_GITHUB_REVIEW_TRUSTED_ASSOCIATIONS` (`OWNER,MEMBER,COLLABORATOR`), non-bot, not in `HEADHUNTER_GITHUB_REVIEW_IGNORE_LOGINS`, plus `/collaborators/{login}/permission` check (`write`/`maintain`/`admin`).
* **3-Channel Approval SHA Drift Gate:** `WAITING_APPROVAL` approvals across REST (`POST /queue/{id}/approve`), WebSocket (`approve`), and Slack (`darwin_approve_sha`) verify `expected_sha` against live HEAD SHA (returning HTTP `409` / `sha_drift` WS error / Slack drift notice on mismatch).

## Feedback Loop, Three-Phase Close & Active Wake-Up

* Brain signals `_headhunter_close_signal.set()` in `_close_and_broadcast()`.
* Headhunter feedback loop wakes on signal or every `poll_interval` and relays wake signals to the poll loop via `_poll_wake_signal`.
* **Three-phase `post_feedback()` (GitLab & GitHub):**
  1. Phase 1: Post summary comment on MR/PR (tracked by `feedback_note_sent`); GitLab fetches live MR state first so stale/closed MRs don't receive redundant feedback.
  2. Phase 2: Dismiss sibling `todo_ids` / swap `darwin-active` -> `darwin-done` and record head SHA (`darwin:gitlab:mr_sha` or `darwin:github:pr_sha`).
  3. Phase 3: Mark `feedback_sent` on the event (supports synthetic `todo_id=None` sweep-triggered events). Transient failures resume cleanly at the incomplete phase without double-posting.
* **Active Event Wake-Up:** When a new push SHA or review feedback arrives for an MR/PR that already has an active or `waiting_approval` event, Headhunter updates `evidence` / appends an `actor=headhunter` evidence turn and wakes Brain instead of creating a duplicate event.

## Dedup & Queue Layers

| Layer | Platform | What it catches | Crash-safe? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `get_active_keys()` (Blackboard active + `waiting_approval` events) | GitLab `(project, mr)`, GitHub `(owner, repo, number)` | Duplicate event for an MR/PR/Issue with an existing active/deferred/`waiting_approval` event | Yes |
| Flow gate (`MAX_ACTIVE_EVENTS`) | both | Concurrent events beyond global WIP cap | Yes |
| Redis FIFO `darwin:gitlab:queue` (+ `:meta`, bounded by `HEADHUNTER_GITLAB_QUEUE_MAX_ENTRIES`) | GitLab | Atomic FIFO persistence across pod restarts when flow gate is closed | Yes |
| `darwin:gitlab:mr_sha` (bounded sweep via `HEADHUNTER_GITLAB_SHA_MAX_ENTRIES`) | GitLab | Re-trigger when a previously completed MR receives a new commit SHA (without `scope=all`) | Yes |
| GitLab todo `mark_as_done` (three-phase close + best-effort terminal/unauthorized cleanup) | GitLab | Re-processing the same todo after event close, or stale terminal/unauthorized todos | Yes |
| GitHub label truth table (`darwin-active` > `darwin-review` > `darwin-queued` > `darwin-done`) + `darwin:github:pr_sha` | GitHub PR | Re-trigger only on a new head SHA after `darwin-done` | Yes |
| `darwin:github:issue:{o}:{r}:{n}` (7d) | GitHub Issue | Re-processing an Issue after a label API failure | Yes |
| `darwin:github:pr_feedback_cursor` + per-item `darwin:github:pr_feedback:{o}:{r}:{pr}:{kind}:{id}` (SET NX, 7d) | GitHub review feedback | At-least-once handling of each review / inline / issue comment, deduped by seen ID | Yes |

## Pure-Redis Pending/Status & Authenticated Operator Controls

* `GET /queue/headhunter/pending`: Pure Redis read merging active + `waiting_approval` Blackboard headhunter events and persisted platform snapshots (`darwin:headhunter:snapshot:{platform}`) — zero live VCS HTTP calls on UI poll; preserves `list[dict]` shape.
* `GET /queue/headhunter/status`: Returns per-platform `{enabled, pending_count, queued_count, last_poll_at, partial_error, breaker}` from Redis/Headhunter with PII-redacted error strings (`<= 200` chars).
* **Operator controls** (guarded by `_require_headhunter_operator` RBAC normalizing `OBS_ADMIN_GROUPS` + `APPROVER_GROUPS`, non-blocking `hh._poll_lock` timeout `5s` -> `409`, 10s debounce, strict membership check in active snapshot):
  * `POST /queue/headhunter/poll`: Debounced poll wake-up.
  * `POST /queue/headhunter/breaker/{platform}/reset`: Reset circuit breaker (`gitlab` | `github`) and wake poll.
  * `POST /queue/headhunter/items/{promote,dismiss,requeue}`: `promote` (`202` async FIFO head bump), `dismiss` (remove from queue / mark todo done / swap labels), `requeue` (clear SHA dedup + re-enqueue).

## Brain Tools: `refresh_gitlab_context` & `refresh_github_context`

Closes the observe-and-react loop (mirrors `re_trigger_aligner`):

* **`refresh_gitlab_context`**: calls `headhunter.refresh_mr_state(event_id)` -> updates `evidence.gitlab_context` + reclassifies `evidence.severity`.
* **`refresh_github_context`**: refreshes live GitHub PR/checks, workflow run (`GitHubRunRef` via `run_id`), or GitHub Issue (`github_issue_context`) state -> updates `evidence.github_context` / `evidence.github_issue_context` + registers background `StateWatcher` subscription.
* **Error handling:** 5xx/429/404 return error dicts; evidence is NOT mutated on error.
* **Registration:** `brain.agents["_headhunter"] = headhunter` in `main.py`.

## Prompt Injection Defense

* Shared untrusted-text sanitization via `sanitize_untrusted_block()` and `sanitize_untrusted_line()` in `src/utils/prompt_sanitize.py` (used by `headhunter.py`, `llm/prompt.py`, and `brain.py`): strips invisible/control characters, removes bounded linear XML prompt fences across Brain + all 7 Headhunter fence tags (`description`, `job_log`, `comments`, `mention_request`, `issue_body`, `review_feedback`, `pr_review_comments`), runs $O(n)$ PII/secret redaction (`src/utils/pii_redaction.py`), defangs case/whitespace-variant `[!call:` directives, and caps length LAST.
* Zero-import `_sanitize_xml_fence()` in `src/agents/headhunter_utils.py` (re-exported by `headhunter.py`) remains for `issue_body` and `review_feedback` blocks.
* Untrusted scalars (`title`, branches, `failed_checks`, `failed_job_names`, `labels`, `changed_files`, `mention_author`) are sanitized via `sanitize_untrusted_line()` (plus quote stripping for XML attributes and JSON-quoting in `_emergency_plan()`).
* `_DESC_SAFETY_CAP` (env: `HEADHUNTER_DESCRIPTION_CAP`, default `100000`) bounds MR/PR descriptions while keeping trailing `### DARWIN Instructions` / `### Bot Instructions` intact.

